\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Chapter two - Vershlingbessern - 20 years before the Dawkins
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 The nation of Ulyssia (Large southern continent not un-like Australia) is invaded by a nation to the north.
\f1 \
\

\f0 The Prime Minister of Ulyssia begs the President of the Union of Capitalist Atlantic States (UCAS), Dunnning Kruger, for military intervention. The President declines to help with \'91boots on the ground\'94 because they are fighting the war against anti-semitism\'94 in 10 theatres of war. Instead Kruger air-bursts 100 nukes over the invading troops and incinerates about 2 million of them. The invasion is defeated, but the land is glowing with radio-activity.
\f1 \

\f0 The UACS charges trillions of credits (or whatever they are - I don\'92t really name the currency) and pretty much bankrupts Ulyssia.Due to his incompetence, the Prime Minister is killed in an in-cabinet coup - his last words \'91et tu Brute\'92. 
\f1 \

\f0 All of the inhabitants of the western province of Western Ulyssia have to evacuate to the eastern \'91states\'92 creating a refugee problem. The locals take advantage of them and they are used pretty much as slaves.
\f1 \

\f0 The Western Province (with hardly anyone there) succeeds and call themselves the new country of Western Ulyssia.
\f1 \

\f0 The eastern part of the country decides to concentrate on manufacturing weapons and change the name of Ulyssia to the Primary Trade Dominion. They will sell weapons to anyone and also develop some nasty biological weapons.
\f1 \

\f0 Introduction to character Jamison Hardy - mega rich, but outwardly not a total arsehole. He appeared to try an protect the refugees from Western Ulyssia. His company manufactures weaponised viruses and were trying to make bio-weapons thata target specific genomes or even specific people.
\f1 \

\f0 A viral plague called \'93The viral cleansing\'94 erupts in Ulyssia - no one knows what happened, but Jamison Hardy disappeared - presumed dead.
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf2 There are a bunch of descriptions that would be better coming from a character that the author, but I haven\'92t got to that yet.
\f1 \cf0 \

\f0 \cf2 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Chapter 3 - Part one - Changing Brooms - 
\f1\b0 \

\f2\b 14 Hours before the nightclub bombing - 9 months before the Dawkins
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 Introduction to Anthony \'93Cracker\'94 Hardy (name will have to change as I think the name Cracker will not resonate with some readers)
\f1 \

\f0 He is cleaning an office and looking out the window at the the skyscrapers jutting upwards out of the \'93layer\'94 (thick permanent layer of cloud/pollution floating about 200m above the sea level.)
\f1 \

\f0 As he looks out of the window, two \cf3 hover-copt\cf0 s crash in mid-air and plummet to through the layer to the ground below. The layer opensup around the burning wrecks and the layer burns for a short time before coalescing. Rich people do not travel on the ground - only by air and if they have to die to avoid mingling with the low-life\'92s on the ground, so be it.
\f1 \

\f0 Cracker point\'92s out the crash to the office workers, but none are interested enough to lookup and no-one would acknowledge the scum-bag cleaner in their midst, just shake their heads that a cleaner would have the effrontery to try to talk with them. 
\f1 \

\f0 Then moves into the office where a level 5 executive had committed suicide. He used a shotgun (not a particle pulse weapon!) and it was a real mess - brain stains. 
\f1 \

\f0 The new occupant of the office, Sarah Jacobson, arrives expecting the office to be ready. She is a stunning blonde. Cracker is a silly child in her presence,but manages to crack a (sort of) joke and gets the office ready for her. He explains he got the cleaning job through a contact in the police, Lieutenant Shakti.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Chapter 4 Lieutenant Shakti -People\'92s Hero 
\f1\b0 \

\f2\b 9 months before the Dawkins
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 Introduction to Lieutenant Shakti - complete moron with no social skills. Born into a Level 5 home he wanted for nothing, but learned nothing instead. He shocked and embarrassed his well-to-do parents by applying to join the police (the public service!) and only just managed to stumble through training. There are some \'93back-story\'94 examples of his abject stupidity.
\f1 \

\f0 Also introduction to his mother Eloise Shakti - super intelligent and ruthless. Managed to get from the lower levels to level 5 by sheer force of will. 
\f1 \

\f0 Narrative about his training in the police academy - how he was truely hopeless , but as a level 5 he could not be failed. The rest of upper level society would not have it. He finally showed some aptitude when he received media training. He was actually good at reading to camera (from auto-cue) and he was sent to take up a position in the \'93Public Affairs Bureau\'94 - dealing with the media. 
\f1 \

\f0 Shakti also has a video streaming show known as Candid Criminal where the cops randomly select a house (of the lower class) and sets up cameras and listening devices. They then recorded everything in the house until someone committed a crime and then they would arrest. The most common crime is \'93Corporate Infidelity\'94, committed either by defaming a manager or breaching employer confidentiality. A very serious offence - doctrinal divergence of this magnitude was punishable by death.
\f1 \

\f0 Guilt is determined by a vote from the viewing audience. It is a very popular show as the upper classes hate the lows and love to see them suffer and die. Shakti introduces a show which is supposed to bring upper class fraudsters etc to book, but in actual fact the execution victim is always a low. (No level 5\'92s were harmed in the making of this show)
\f1 \

\f0 Voting by the audience is monitored by the PTD to ensure the upper classes don\'92t feel any compassion or deliver mercy. Indulging in compassion is moral weakness.
\f1 \

\f0 (A TV show that includes executions? What a trope!)
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Chapter 5 - The Gyges Disc 
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 Return to Cracker leaving the Sarah\'92s office floor. 
\f1 \

\f0 He leaves via the \'93tradesman\'92s\'94 elevator, but halfway down a level 5 dude (later it becomes clear this person is a company agent) gets in the lift and takes them back up to level 216 and gets out. 
\f1 \

\f0 He harrasses and threatens Sarah about the previous occupant of the office (Mr Lee) and wants to know where all of his property is. She stares him down and tells him the cleaner had just left with all of the rubbish. His mantra is \'93
\f3\i I am not human. I am the biological manifestation of the company\'92s will. In the name of stability I destabilize. In the name of order I deliver chaos. In the name of life I bring death.\'94 
\f1\i0 \

\f0 The agent runs out to catch the cleaner.
\f1 \

\f0 Sarah reports the matter to security, but they are all watching Shakti\'92s show and she can\'92t get hold of them. She hacks the surveillance system, but is unable to locate the agent anywhere. There is no footage of him entering her office. She realises he must be a crazy company agent and she had sent him after the cleaner. 
\f1 \

\f0 \
At street level Cracker wanders out and trips over a man who had died on the sidewalk. Other pedstristrian walk around the body as if not to notice. The dead guy is dressed like an L.5. But has grubby fingers and dirty fingernails - definately not L.5. Cracker seaches the body and steals anything he can find.
\f1 \

\f0 Around the corner are two operational support officers who decide to pick up the body eventhough the agent has not re-appeared from the building. They approach the body and tell Cracker to piss off. The support officers pick up the body.
\f1 \

\f0 Cracker then leaves the area via the giant security gates that lead from the \'93Management District\'94 to \'93The Pale\'94. He has a run in with a security guard who is trying to get him to upgrade his security ID from a tattoo to a brain implant. The Security Guard gets kickbacks from the brain implant mob for sending clients to them, but Cracker calls him on it and is finally let through.
\f1 \

\f0 \
Description of The Pale - dark horrible ghetto with a crime rate so unconscionably high the police never visit. Law enforcement is engage in shielding the rich from the poor, not protecting the poor from each other. 
\f4\i \'93
\f3 In the Primary Trade Dominion, egalitarians were those who ate eagle.\'94 
\f1\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 - - -
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 Sarah is concerned about the fact she sent an intelligence agent after Cracker and interrogates every data base trying to find out about him, but there is not much information - which is suspicious - entries had recently been deleted. She finds a couple of fines for drunk and disorderly (at the Stick it Inn) and that is about it.
\f1 \

\f0 She has to go to her promotional medical exam - which she passess. She is amused that the medical report notes she is not pregnant.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Chapter 6 - Pre-emtive Reciprocity 
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 The agent burst out of the building and onto the street, particle pistol in hand, but no-one is there.
\f1 \

\f0 No meat wagon - No Blank (a blank is a terminally ill person who is recruited for assassination on the promise their family would be taken care of after his/her death)
\f1 \

\f0 Worse still, he had misplaced a Gyges Disc. (Gyges disc - also called a cloak - is a small metal disc of unknown origin that makes the holder of the disc invisible to electronic surveillance.
\f1 \

\f0 His boss is not impressed - he has lost the disc, the blank and they don\'92t know where the operational support guys are.
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Chapter 7 - The Blank
\f1\b0 \

\f2\b 14 hours before the bombing
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 The blank was loaded onto the van by the operational support guys and taken to a morgue. They were diverted to the public morgue in an ultra-rich health and retreat area of the city and had spent a great deal of time getting through customs at the security gate. (There is an explanation as to why there is a public facility in an ultra rich area)
\f1 \

\f0 The blank, Emil Kalheri, was a level one labourer who had terminal testicular cancer and was recruited by the \'93Department of Pre-emptive Reciprocity and Proactive euthanasia\'94
\f1 \

\f0 He was recruited to assassinate Mr Lee and agreed after he was told Mr Lee was a paedophile. The agent, Agent Jones (his first name is Agent) arrives at the morgue and finally located the blank, but is not happy because the gyges disc is not with his property and he concludes the cleaner has the disc.
\f1 \

\f0 He then attempts to locate Cracker, but also finds there is nothing (or virtually nothing) on the cleaner. He thinks the cleaner might be from an unknown faction because only agents are afforded that degree of anonymity. 
\f1 \

\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Chapter 8 - Hot time in the ol\'92 town - 
\f1\b0 \

\f2\b 4 hours before the bombing
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 (Sorry this chapter is trope-city)
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 Cracker gets home to find his live in partner is angry because he had not put them up for \'91allocation\'92 (marriage). She physically attacks him and with martial arts skills kicks the shit out of him and informs him she had place herself up for random allocation and had been allocated to James Marrin, BComm L.3.
\f1 \

\f0 She tell him she faked them all and then left. Cracker then arranges to go out with his mates for a celebratory drink at the \'93Stick it Inn\'94 nightclub. It is an \'91open\'92 premises in that any level person could enter, but dress regulations were so strict only the rich could get in, unless, like Cracker, you have low connections everywhere.
\f1 \

\f0 His mates were waiting for him - Halo, Major, Abe. Halo was at the table staring at the crown trying to identify his net conquest. He was prolific in jagging women with a minimum of talk, if any. 
\f1 \

\f0 Halo id\'92s a woman and heads off to pick her up, but unusually he is back in double quick time, tail between his legs. The woman had rejected him outright.
\f4\i  \'93Dykes, they\'92re all fucking dykes\'94 he says to the boys at the table.
\f1\i0 \

\f0 The woman who rejected him approaches the table - \'93Oh fuck, its her.\'94 The woman is Sarah and she is looking for Cracker. Shortly after Halo spots another woman and he is gone. Major and Abe go to the bar and come back with drinks just before a bomb goes off obliterating the bar. Cracker and Sarah manage to crawl out of the rubble.
\f1 \

\f0 Cracker tells her they must leave. Anyone found near a terrorist incident will be arrested and interrogated, no matter who they are. They are smoldering and blackened with some serious cuts and bruises, but manage to hobble away. They get out of the immediate area, but realise their appearance will give them away. Sarah manages to hack (computer) their way into a public hygiene facility to clean up and wash the evidence of the explosion off them. Cracker tells her the water is tested for drugs, explosives, heavy metals & contaminents and they must, somehow, block the drains. 
\f1 \

\f0 The drains are massive and Cracker chucks towels and chairs and anything he can get his hands on to block the drain. He is assists by a madman who jumps atop of the pile and starts calling for his \'93Comrads\'94 to gather around. (He slips and gets stuck in the drain)
\f1 \

\f0 They each enter the facility - Cracker in the mens section, Sarah in the womens section. Sarah breaks into the control room of the facility and diverts the flow of the water (she does not know where) and also warms the water up 5 degrees. The shower are banks of cages, attached to the wall and stacked on top of one another. The top row get hot clean water, the lower cages just get what drips down from above.
\f1 \

\f0 They decide to go for the drink they did not get to have at the Stickett Inn and head for \'93The Quarter\'94. 
\f1 \

\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Chapter 9 - A Big Crush
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 When Cracker and Sarah get back to street level, there is a massive crowd . The Police have diverted everyone away from the bombing and have created a crush. 
\f1 \

\f0 Bit of back story of how Cracker knows Shakti. Cracker was on duty at a crush a few years earlier. A crowd of people had been crushed to death, but rigour-mortis had locked the crowd (mostly standing) together and they had to wedge the bodies apart to removed. They finally decided to use a big front end loader.
\f1 \

\f0 Cracker ducks off for a spew and finds Shakti vomiting on the ground. 
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 - - - 
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Chapter 10 - Suicide Homicide
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0  - 2 Hours after the bombing
\f1 \

\f0  (May be out of whack/time with the rest of the story)
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 Shakti is asleep and having a dream about his blonde dream woman. He is on a beach with pure white sand and crystal blue water. Something that no-one alive had ever seen. He ws walking along the beach holding the hand of dream-woman when she suddenly turns in to his mother and she tries to drag him off to college so he can become an accountant.
\f1 \

\f0 He is then awoken by a holo of the Commissioner of Police hovering over him. The Commissioner abuses him for his lackluster investigation into the Lee death. 
\f4\i \'93Did I not send you to investigate a murder?\'94 
\f0\i0 Shakti had written it off as a suicide. 
\f1 \

\f0 He is informed that there has been a coordinated terrorist incident where they had let off a bomb and then diverted the water away from the subsequent fires. Shakti think he is being given a terrorist incident to investigate but is disappointed when he is placed on clean-up duty at the public hygiene facility - level 5\'92s have had recyc diverted as drinking water!!!
\f1 \

\f0 Shakti, is hated by his peers and he know he will get no assistance from them. He turns to his only friend - Cracker.
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 - - -
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 Cracker and Sarah found themselves in the middle of a crush with no hope of getting out. Shakti contacts by mobile device and tells Cracker he needs him. Cracker tells him he can\'92t help, he is in a crush. Shakti tells him to standby he will be there shortly. Shakti turns up in a \cf3 hover-copt\cf0  and decends upon the crowd, who manage to make sufficent space. An armed police officer jumps out of the copter and gives Cracker and Sarah \'93forensic suits\'94 and tells them to get in the copter. He turns to the crowd and shoots a number of the crown dead. Shakti tries asks if it was necessary to kill people he is told wounding them wrecks your shot to kill ratio - and
\f4\i  \'91don\'92t worry I only shot white people so it wasn\'92t racist or anything.\'92
\f1\i0 \

\f0 They take off and Shakti briefs them on the job - terrorists have bombed a club and diverted the water away from the fire. Cracker and Sarah immediately afraid of being found out. 
\f1 \

\f0 They go back to the public hygiene facility - flooded with city workers unable to locate the drain. Cracker wades in. Sarah goes to the control room where city engineers and computer geeks are failing to restore the correct water flow. Sarah completes the task, but the blokes won\'92t give her any credit. 
\f1 \

\f0 Cracker unblocks the drain and manages to float the body of the guy who fell into the drain and got stuck. He floats him to the stairs and says to Shakti, \'93Here\'92s your terrorist.\'94
\f1 \

\f0 Shakti arranges a \cf3 hover-copt\cf0  to take them away telling them \'93Neither of you were here.\'94
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0  - - -
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Chapter 11 - A Big Bang for the Big Bang
\f1\b0 \

\f2\b (At the time of the bombing - we have gone back a couple of hours)
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 Halo had seen the woman on the other side of the bar, just minutes before the explosion. He picks her up in double quick time and they are out the door. They kiss and are knocked over by the explosion. The go back to her house.
\f1 \

\f0 The woman, AVI, is an agent from the Department of Pre-emtive reciprocity and Proactive Euthenasia, who has been sent to place a bomb in the Stick it Inn (it is uncertain, but Cracker may have been the target).
\f1 \

\f0 They go back to her place - she plans to kill him, he plans to kill her. She is an assassin and he is a serial killer. (He is later identified as the \'93Nightclub Stalker/killer\'94)
\f1 \

\f0 The have sex and he kills her with a special knife/blade he had made. It is hollow in the middle so the blood spurts really high. However, because he stabbed her through the heart, the blood stopped pumping after a short time. He was not satiated and he goes out to find another victim.
\f1 \

\f0 He finds himself in the same crush as Cracker and Sarah. He stabs a few people and melts back into the crowd, but them he sights Cracker ex girlfriend, Angela. She is crying because her boyfriend suddenly disappeared and she thought he may have been trampled. Halo knows he must have stabbed him and he is greatly amused. He tells Angela they are is real trouble, but he might be able to get them off the street. He takes her back to Avi\'92s apartment.
\f4\i  \'91He thought himself a simple man with simple needs \'96 if he had a girl to fuck and stab, he was sweet.\'92 
\f1\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f5\i\b \cf0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Chapter 12 - Dark Forces 
\f1\i0\b0 \

\f5\i\b 75 Minutes after the bombing - Immediately following the phone call with Shakti (Chapter 10)
\f1\i0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 The Commissioner of Police hangs up the phone on Shakti and makes a call to the CEO telling him Shakti fucked it up more than they had hoped. He called it suicide and went back to bed. No evidence collected.
\f1 \

\f0 The CEO is told the blank completed the job, made it look like suicide, but lost the gyges disc in the process. The blank had gone missing. The CEO wants the blank (Emil Kalheri) located as a priority.
\f1 \

\f0 The Commissioner was amoral and completely untrustworthy - making him a model public servant. He was a genius with malleable ethics. He contacts his most competent investigator,, Det Supt Hayley Lanning - she is one of the few honest cops on the force.
\f1 \

\f0 She is not happy about being put on a missing persons gig. She is in charge of the \'93Nightclub Killer\'94 investigation and did not want to drop it to find a L1 labourer.
\f1 \

\f0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Chapter 13 - The Elvi (Pronounced El-Vye)
\f1\b0 \

\f2\b 3 hours after the bombing
\f1\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 Sarah and Cracker can\'92t let the pilot know where they live so they get dropped off in the Quarter to see the Elvi.
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\qc\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 - - - 
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Cloning the Arts
\f0\b0  - Flashback 20years before the Dawkins. Dr Linus Grawling was a geneticist and music devotee. He hated modern music (rap) and spent years undertaking questionable (and criminal) research and scouring the globe to gather together the DNA of iconic musicians - raiding mausoleums, crypts, graves, ash filled urns. He cloned and cloned but found only one DNA strand that would readily lend itself to cloning. The DNA of a long lost singer - named Elvis. No-one knew his last name.
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 Cloned Elvis\'92 became pretty much mandatory for bars, restaurants, nightclubs etc. Every one of those type of businesses had one Elvis, some had nothing but Elvis employees. You had to keep them away from fatty food, guns, bizarre fashion and religion. For some reason the Elvi are especially susceptible to spiritual manipulation. If they were introduced to religion their warranty was void.
\f1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 Vegas Show
\f0\b0  - The \cf3 hover-copt\cf0  dropped them in the quarter and they head to a bar. Elvis\'92s and Elvine\'92s are notoriously intolerant of the impolite and it is advisable to be as polite as possible when dealing with an Elvis. They were served by and Elvine and seated in a booth. From there they drink hard and watch the Elvi sing and dance in what was called a Vegas show.
\f1 \

\f2\b Hangover
\f0\b0  - Cracker is suffering the worst effects of a night with the Elvi. Very hungover.
\f6  \'91
\f4\i His blackened left eye was firmly closed shut and continually seeped a dilute blood-ooze that trickled over the collection of lumps, cuts, scratches and bruises that together contrived to construct something not too dissimilar to a face.\'92
\f1\i0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\partightenfactor0

\f0 \cf0 Sarah is in his apartment, but they did not do the deed. He is below her station and she wishes to remain a virgin. 
\f1 \

\f0 While Cracker was asleep, Sarah had been surfing the link - the only news is the bombing and the coordinated diversion of water away from the fire. There was news that a terrorist had been caught by Lieutenant Shakti.
\f1 \

\f0 Sarah is concerned that Shakti can\'92t be trusted. Cracker tells her Shakti is not capable of self sacrifice, but he will never tell anyone a cleaner helped him - his mother would never let him live it down. 
\f1 \

\f0 She tells him about the visit at her office from a company agent. Cracker saw him on the elevator. She shows him the surveillance footage she had downloaded, there is no sign of the Agent, entering or leaving the office. Cracker has a look and notices that there is no trace of him leaving the office either - footage of him entering, but not leaving. Sarah did not notice this and he teases her about being smarter that her and then curls into a foetal position due to the excruciating hangover he is suffering through. He tells her where all the spoils from the previously day are and then crashes out. 
\f1 \

\f0 He wakes in fright, thinking that she had left, but she is still there and has looked at all the stuff he had knocked off the day before. Among the items are a wallet with id in the name of Emil Kalheri and a shiny silver disc the size of a thumbnail and a general access chip - will open any electronic-locked door in the dominion until expiration.
\f1 \

